Here is the commit message:
BulkLoader: Allow zero user types to be loaded

This patch fixes a bug which prevented the loader
from working with keyspaces containing no user types.

Signed-off-by: Duarte Nunes <duarte@scylladb.com>
Message-Id: <1462364882-31186-1-git-send-email-duarte@scylladb.com>

Here is the root cause:
In the fixed-point recursive algorithm of `loadUserTypes`, when the initial `udts` collection passed in was empty (i.e., a keyspace had zero user-defined types), the method would still proceed to the check `notLoaded.size() == udts.size()`. Since both `notLoaded` and `udts` were empty (0 == 0), this condition evaluated to `true`, causing the method to incorrectly throw a `RuntimeException("Unable to load user types []")` even though there was no actual failure—there simply were no UDTs to load. The method lacked a base case to handle the legitimate scenario of an empty input collection, conflating "no progress made while trying to load types" with "no types to load in the first place."

Here is the patch:
         // forward progress.
         private static void loadUserTypes(Collection<UserType> udts, KSMetaData ks) {
+            if (udts.isEmpty()) {
+                return;
+            }
             LinkedList<UserType> notLoaded = new LinkedList<UserType>();
             for (UserType ut : udts) {
                 try {
                     ArrayList<ByteBuffer> fieldNames = new ArrayList<ByteBuffer>(ut.getFieldNames().size());
                     ArrayList<AbstractType<?>> fieldTypes = new ArrayList<AbstractType<?>>();
                     for (UserType.Field f : ut) {
                         fieldNames.add(ByteBufferUtil.bytes(f.getName()));
                         fieldTypes.add(getCql3Type(f.getType()).prepare(ks.name).getType());
                     }
                     ks.userTypes.addType(new org.apache.cassandra.db.marshal.UserType(
                         ks.name, ByteBufferUtil.bytes(ut.getTypeName()), fieldNames, fieldTypes));
                 } catch (Exception e) {
                     System.out.println(e);
                     notLoaded.addFirst(ut);
                 }
             }
             if (notLoaded.size() == udts.size()) {
                 throw new RuntimeException("Unable to load user types " + notLoaded);
             }
-            if (notLoaded.size() > 0) {
-                loadUserTypes(notLoaded, ks);
-            }
+            loadUserTypes(notLoaded, ks);
         }



